On Fri, 13 Oct 2006 20:40:49 +0100, Ugly Newt wrote:

> AFAICS, the only thing you can do in Ludios is to (s)earch several times
> on each square, and do everything you can to max your dexterity (or use
> the rogue Quest artifact, with a long wait between attempts) before
> disarming mines.  That's not a puzzle-like subgame at all.

A confused scroll of gold detection will reveal all traps on the level.
A wand of secret door detection or spell of detect unseen will reveal
traps within a certain radius; zap one at the door to the treasure room,
make your way to the center, and zap it again.

Once you've detected all the land mines, you can levitate and float back
and forth through the room until you've set the last one off.  Or just try
to disarm them and take your lumps when one goes kaboom.  You'll get over
your wounded legs soon enough.

